A move whose joints leave their travel between its ends is refused before
it is sent, not stopped on the soft limit partway through it.

5axiskins with a 400 mm pivot, the head laid over to B90 by a joint move,
the tool tip held while C turns, so that the carriage swings round the tip
at the pivot length plus the tool length; C-90 puts it at Y+ that radius,
against joint 1's MAX_LIMIT of 400.  A tool length of 0.05 makes the swing
from C-5 to C-175 peak 0.05 past the travel at C-90, between two samples
1.2 inside it: the move is refused, asked again it is refused again, and
moves inside the travel still go, turning the other way among them; a
move ending past the travel is refused for its end.  At -0.05 the same
swing peaks 0.05 inside and runs; at 100 the samples themselves are past.
With the head upright an arc whose ends are inside the travel and whose
top is past it is refused, the same arc the other way round runs.  A
program fails on the line of the swing with no joint past its limit, and
run from the line after it, which only steps over the swing, it runs.
